title: Workflow documentation for SMV

!!! Titles:
* Sarga(#).(shloka#)
**``example: Sarga1.15``

!!! Tags:
*shloka(#) tiddlers are tagged with sarga(#) ie. belong to category
* sarga(#) tiddlers are tagged with SMV  ie. belong to category

!!! Views:
*SMV is list filter of all sargas (links only / transclusion : undecided)
*sarga(#) is transclusion of all shlokas with corresponding tag; in detail/summary. Shloka is presented as summary. Artha with transclusion of fields in a table is 'detail' view.

!!! Operation:
*if artha tiddler doesn't exist:
** copy shloka, r-click > services > ``open shloka URL`` and ``copy to Clipboard`` the result. 
** open link to create artha tiddler, paste into ``create padartha fields`` and save
** add additional grammar notes to ``kp_व्याकर्ण_विशेषः`` field

!!! Backend:
``kp editTemplate addfields``
contains code assigning names/fields to each shloka-artha. [[link|$:/core/ui/EditTemplate/fields]]

``show-kpfields-template``
contains code to display field content in body of tiddler (formatted). [[link|kp show SKS fields template]] 

same code should be used in sarga tiddlers to show interactive meaning. 